In this conversation, James inquired about the type of rock sling called a "slingshot" or "catapult," which can be used to shoot projectiles by pulling back on one end. He considered using it to kill or knock out mice but was guided toward the effectiveness and safety of the method. I advised that while a slingshot can be used for target practice, it may not be effective for controlling mice due to their quick movements and the potential for damage indoors. I recommended more humane methods for rodent control, such as traps and reducing food sources, while highlighting the importance of safety when using a slingshot outdoors.
